            <div xml:id="d769">

                <pb facs="0950" n="860" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg860"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2161: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Chargé of the Legation in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-20T10:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">February 20,
                                1920—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>21. Congress has declared state of siege or martial law in southern departments
                    including Tegucigalpa. Recruiting has begun to send additional troops to the
                    Nicaraguan boundary. Public speaker of last night openly declared revolutionary
                    movement from Nicaragua to be with tacit consent of the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
